cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file,
  and state the version you used.
title: "FreqProb: A Python library for probability smoothing and frequency-based estimation"
abstract: >-
  FreqProb is a Python library for scoring observation probabilities from
  frequency counts. It provides a range of smoothing methods, from Laplace and
  Lidstone to Simple Good-Turing and Kneser-Ney, behind a single consistent
  interface, together with sample-coverage and bias-corrected entropy
  estimators, for natural language processing, information retrieval,
  ecology, and statistical modeling.
type: software
